# Project: Pokémon Mezastar Trade-Fairness Tool

A tool where two people each pick a batch of Mezastar tags to trade; it sums a transparent
point value per side and judges fairness. Audience includes kids — keep UX simple and scoring
explainable. Standalone project, NOT part of the `pokemon-mezastar` PWA (shares data only).
Region scope: Taiwan (zh-TW); stats identical to Japanese release.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript **strict**, Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (auth + Postgres for per-user collections/favorites) — login is required
- next-intl (zh-TW + EN, all strings externalized)
- Zod at every data boundary
- Fuse.js for EN + zh-TW fuzzy search
- Vercel deploy

## Hard rules
- TypeScript strict; avoid `any` (require a written justification if unavoidable).
- Validate every external input and API response with Zod.
- Never hardcode user-facing zh/en strings in components — use next-intl message files.
- Never commit official Pokémon tag images to git. Images live in a storage bucket.
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`).
- Record consequential decisions as ADRs in `docs/adr/`.
